=== HONESTY_COVENANT ===
Files modified by this prompt (allowlist with variance applied):
  migrations/000174_fsm_live.up.sql
  migrations/000174_fsm_live.down.sql
  .github/prompts/db-refactor/logs/phase-42-0035-mig-create-fsm-live.log

What this migration does, in plain English:
  - Defensively drops fsm_transitions and vehicle_live_state if they
    already exist (idempotent re-apply against test databases that
    still hold stray legacy objects).
  - Creates fsm_transitions: append-only state-machine transition log,
    one row per state change per FSM per vehicle.
      id          BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY
      vehicle_id  BIGINT NOT NULL
      ts          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL
      fsm_name    TEXT NOT NULL  -- 'drive_state' | 'charge_state' | ...
      from_state  TEXT           -- nullable; first-observed transition
      to_state    TEXT NOT NULL  -- destination is required
      trigger     TEXT           -- nullable; field that drove the change
      details     JSONB          -- nullable; FSM-specific structured ctx
    Indexes:
      fsm_transitions_vehicle_ts (vehicle_id, ts DESC)
      fsm_transitions_fsm_ts     (fsm_name,   ts DESC)
  - Creates vehicle_live_state: durable mirror of the L2 (Redis) HSET
    `vehicle:{vehicleID}:signals`, used for restart recovery.
      vehicle_id      BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
      updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL
      drive_state     TEXT
      charge_state    TEXT
      last_lat        DOUBLE PRECISION
      last_lng        DOUBLE PRECISION
      last_speed_mps  DOUBLE PRECISION  -- SI: meters per second
      soc_pct         REAL              -- 0-100
      odometer_m      DOUBLE PRECISION  -- SI: meters
      battery_level   INT               -- Tesla 0-100 UI field
      inside_temp_c   REAL              -- SI: Celsius
      outside_temp_c  REAL              -- SI: Celsius
      locked          BOOLEAN
      sentry_mode     BOOLEAN
      full_state      JSONB             -- periodic Redis HSET snapshot
    Single PK index (no secondary indexes — vehicle_id is the only
    natural query key for this table).
  - Both tables are intentionally NOT hypertables:
      vehicle_live_state is keyed by vehicle (one row per vehicle, ever)
      and would have nothing to chunk on; fsm_transitions has too few
      rows per vehicle (~1000s/year) to benefit from chunk-based
      partitioning. They live as plain regular tables.
  - Applies a TABLE COMMENT and per-column COMMENTs documenting the
    layered live-state contract on both tables.
  - down.sql drops both new tables CASCADE (forward-only rollback —
    no legacy schema to restore).
  - Honesty covenants 1-10: unchanged.

Allowed files this prompt (with variance applied):
  migrations/000174_fsm_live.up.sql
  migrations/000174_fsm_live.down.sql
  .github/prompts/db-refactor/logs/phase-42-0035-mig-create-fsm-live.log

=== SCHEMA ===
migrations/000174_fsm_live.up.sql defines, in order:

  -- defensive cleanup
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS fsm_transitions    CASCADE;
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS vehicle_live_state CASCADE;

  -- fsm_transitions
  CREATE TABLE fsm_transitions (
    id         BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    vehicle_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
    ts         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    fsm_name   TEXT NOT NULL,
    from_state TEXT,
    to_state   TEXT NOT NULL,
    trigger    TEXT,
    details    JSONB
  );
  CREATE INDEX fsm_transitions_vehicle_ts
    ON fsm_transitions (vehicle_id, ts DESC);
  CREATE INDEX fsm_transitions_fsm_ts
    ON fsm_transitions (fsm_name, ts DESC);
  COMMENT ON TABLE  fsm_transitions IS '...';
  COMMENT ON COLUMN fsm_transitions.* IS '...'  (7 column comments)

  -- vehicle_live_state
  CREATE TABLE vehicle_live_state (
    vehicle_id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY,
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    drive_state    TEXT,
    charge_state   TEXT,
    last_lat       DOUBLE PRECISION,
    last_lng       DOUBLE PRECISION,
    last_speed_mps DOUBLE PRECISION,
    soc_pct        REAL,
    odometer_m     DOUBLE PRECISION,
    battery_level  INT,
    inside_temp_c  REAL,
    outside_temp_c REAL,
    locked         BOOLEAN,
    sentry_mode    BOOLEAN,
    full_state     JSONB
  );
  COMMENT ON TABLE  vehicle_live_state IS '...';
  COMMENT ON COLUMN vehicle_live_state.* IS '...'  (15 column comments)

migrations/000174_fsm_live.down.sql is the inverse:
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS fsm_transitions    CASCADE;
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS vehicle_live_state CASCADE;

Substring checks the gate runs against up.sql (PowerShell -match,
regex semantics):
  'CREATE TABLE fsm_transitions'      -> match (line 47)
  'CREATE TABLE vehicle_live_state'   -> match (line 80)
  'from_state'                        -> match (column + COMMENT)
  'to_state'                          -> match (column + COMMENT)
  'full_state'                        -> match (column + COMMENT)
  'vehicle_id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY'     -> match (line 81)

The vehicle_live_state column-list inside the prompt's CREATE TABLE
is intentionally formatted with single-space tokens between
`vehicle_id`, `BIGINT`, and `PRIMARY KEY` so the gate's bare-string
regex (single-space tokens) matches without extra-whitespace
considerations.

