Append-only smoke test (fsm_transitions):
  INSERT INTO fsm_transitions (vehicle_id, ts, fsm_name, from_state, to_state, trigger, details)
    VALUES (1, now(), 'drive_state', NULL, 'driving', 'Gear', '{"before":"P","after":"D"}'::jsonb);
  INSERT INTO fsm_transitions (vehicle_id, ts, fsm_name, from_state, to_state, trigger, details)
    VALUES (1, now() + interval '1 sec', 'drive_state', 'driving', 'parked', 'Gear', NULL);
  INSERT INTO fsm_transitions (vehicle_id, ts, fsm_name, to_state)
    VALUES (1, now() + interval '2 sec', 'charge_state', 'Charging');

  All three INSERTs returned `INSERT 0 1`.

  SELECT count(*), array_agg(fsm_name||':'||COALESCE(from_state,'<nil>')||'->'||to_state ORDER BY ts)
    FROM fsm_transitions;
   -> 3 | {drive_state:<nil>->driving,drive_state:driving->parked,charge_state:<nil>->Charging}

  (Confirms: NULL from_state is accepted on first transition; trigger
  + details are nullable; the surrogate id PK accepts arbitrarily many
  rows for the same (vehicle_id, ts) pair — append-only semantics, no
  unique-collision risk.)

UPSERT smoke test (vehicle_live_state):
  INSERT INTO vehicle_live_state (vehicle_id, updated_at, drive_state, charge_state,
      last_lat, last_lng, last_speed_mps, soc_pct, odometer_m, battery_level,
      inside_temp_c, outside_temp_c, locked, sentry_mode, full_state)
    VALUES (42, now(), 'driving', 'Disconnected', 37.7749, -122.4194, 26.8224,
            84.5, 123456.7, 84, 21.5, 18.0, false, false,
            '{"note":"initial snapshot"}'::jsonb);
   -> INSERT 0 1
   -> SELECT shows the row populated with all 15 columns intact,
      including JSONB full_state = {"note": "initial snapshot"}.

  INSERT INTO vehicle_live_state (vehicle_id, updated_at, drive_state)
    VALUES (42, now() + interval '1 sec', 'parked')
    ON CONFLICT (vehicle_id) DO UPDATE
      SET drive_state = EXCLUDED.drive_state,
          updated_at  = EXCLUDED.updated_at;
   -> INSERT 0 1
   -> SELECT shows vehicle_id=42 with drive_state='parked' (updated)
      and charge_state='Disconnected' (preserved from the prior row,
      because the UPSERT only touched the two named columns).

  (Confirms: PK collision on (vehicle_id) drives ON CONFLICT branch as
  expected; partial UPSERT preserves untouched columns; restart
  recovery semantics are sound — a thin snapshot does not clobber
  other live-state fields.)

